        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF141 adds support for clearing <code class=\"notranslate\">bfcache</code> using <code class=\"notranslate\">Clear-Site-Data: cache</code> HTTP header in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1930501\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1930501</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note, and mentions that it might be cleared in the <code class=\"notranslate\">cache</code> directive option.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3166056275\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40020\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40020/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40020\">#40020</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40033",
            "title": "FF141 Relnote: Clear-Site-Data: cache clears bfcache",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-23T07:41:08.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-23T01:00:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112726619?u=6d16930d0e2054b2b458c320f6f8b85b602b8da2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The paragraph that aimed to be fixed contained 2 issues:</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Logical error: there is no 'success'/'error' events on  DOM event type property, according to official specification <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The explanation text was just hard to read and focus, so it is a bit simplified and more concised</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I made this change, so the developers do not be confused with unexpected 'error' / 'success' DOM event types</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40025",
            "title": "Fixing explanations of onsuccess/onerror listeners for IndexedDB",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-22T17:56:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-22T15:44:53.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "afonyaa",
                "url": "https://github.com/afonyaa"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70334120?u=3d664e6255d584f51d38a8d37f3a788358b6797d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Clarified how the <code class=\"notranslate\">sizes</code> attribute works with <code class=\"notranslate\">srcset</code>, including a detailed explanation and example of how it helps the browser choose the optimal image based on screen size and device pixel ratio. Also added notes on browser-specific behavior when resizing.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">sizes</code> attribute was previously referenced but not properly introduced or explained, which could confuse readers unfamiliar with how responsive images work. This change helps users understand <em>why</em> <code class=\"notranslate\">sizes</code> is important, how it affects image selection from <code class=\"notranslate\">srcset</code>, and what to expect across different browsers.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/source#sizes\" rel=\"nofollow\">MDN <code class=\"notranslate\">sizes</code> docs</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/picture\" rel=\"nofollow\">Picture Element</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #39689.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3091677915\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39689\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/39689/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39689\">#39689</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40017",
            "title": "Added example for sizes attribute",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-21T20:31:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-21T20:20:46.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "jvlavan",
                "url": "https://github.com/jvlavan"
            }
        },
